    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0301" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg233"/>

                <head>Mr. Dix to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-02-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 19,1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose a translation of the parts of the
                    annual exposition of the condition of the French empire, presented by the
                    government to the Senate and Corps Legislatif, relating to the United States and
                    Mexico. The expression of good feeling in respect to the former and the
                    unconditional abandonment of the latter are a true index of the more general
                    feeling which exists here on both subjects. The paragraphs referred to will be
                    found on pages 302 and 303 of the “Exposé” which I will send you in the despatch
                    bag on Friday. It is too bulky for the mail.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN A. DIX.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d246-a1.xml" xpointer="d246-a1"/>
            </div>
